dialect protocol
protocol svg.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.svg
start record

# P2-FG3: REAL binary op frame, replacing F6's `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op` -- see that file's `#region OpCodecs` for the
# upgraded implementation). `SvgMutation` is a genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed a
# recursive `XmlNode`/`NodePath` (a `Vec<usize>`-backed path) and, for `SetSnapshot`, a full
# recursive `SvgSnapshot` -- no `DslField` impl exists or can exist for a data-carrying enum
# (confirmed live, F6's own recon), so the generic `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body`
# layout genuinely does not fit. Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`store::OP_BINARY_FORMAT`
# convention) + `tag u8` (the `SvgMutation` variant ordinal, 0-10, same order
# `print_svg_mutation`'s keyword match uses: no-mutation, set-snapshot, set-declaration,
# set-doctype, insert-element, remove-element, set-element-name, set-attribute, set-text,
# set-view-box, set-transform) as two REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own path/index/node/
# view-box/transform payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain.
#
# The recursive payload itself is real LEB128-varint-framed binary (`enc_xml_node_bin`/
# `enc_node_path_bin`/`enc_view_box_bin`/`enc_transform_list_bin` in the same `🦀️component.rs`,
# reusing `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/`store::ByteReader`) -- NOT re-modeled field-by-field
# here because `Prim::Ref` (the only construct that could describe `XmlNode`'s self-recursion at
# the protocol-dialect level) unconditionally errors during `walk_protocol` (the
# `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` mechanism gap, hit by every stdio pilot's own recursive
# mutation/diff payload). This is the same honest-boundary treatment the plan itself prescribes for
# a compressed payload segment -- opaque at the protocol layer, genuinely structured (and
# round-trip-tested) at the Rust layer.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
